{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            549,
            556
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The box"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 1,
      "position": [
        547,
        556
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            558,
            749
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "A page is a box inside a box. The outer one is the sheet, given here as an\nexplicit pair rather than a paper name, and the inner one is what is left after\nthe margins are taken off each edge."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        558,
        749
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            754,
            776
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Four units, four edges"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 2,
      "position": [
        751,
        776
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            778,
            999
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The four margins are written in four different units on purpose: millimetres,\npoints, and inches all have to arrive at the same measure, and an edge that\nquietly fell back to a default would move every line on every page."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        778,
        999
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1004,
            1030
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "What the running heads say"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 2,
      "position": [
        1001,
        1030
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1032,
            1323
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The header is off on the first page and on from the second, so the first page\nof a document is not stamped like a continuation of something. Each slot is\ninterpolated once per page and drawn as an artifact, outside the structure\ntree, because a running head is furniture rather than content."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        1032,
        1323
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1327,
            1345
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The second chapter"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 1,
      "position": [
        1325,
        1345
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1347,
            1653
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Page numbering restarts here, which is the whole point of naming a level: the\ncount is a property of the chapter, not of the sheet, and the footer has to\nfollow it. Roman numerals are spelled out from a table rather than asked of the\nhost locale, so this document numbers its pages the same way everywhere."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        1347,
        1653
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1658,
            1689
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "A table of contents comes first"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 2,
      "position": [
        1655,
        1689
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1691,
            1910
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The contents are emitted ahead of the body and take a break after themselves,\nso the body opens on a page of its own. Entries go two levels deep, which is\nwhy the third-level heading below is absent from the list above."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        1691,
        1910
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1916,
            1935
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Not in the contents"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 3,
      "position": [
        1912,
        1935
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1937,
            2149
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Depth is a promise about the list, not about the document. This heading is\nstill a heading, still bookmarked, and still in the structure tree; it is only\nmissing from the page the reader was given to navigate by."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        1937,
        2149
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            2154,
            2168
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The last of it"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 2,
      "position": [
        2151,
        2168
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            2170,
            2363
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The final paragraph exists so that the second chapter is long enough to need a\npage the first one did not, and so the total in the footer is a number that had\nto be counted rather than guessed."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        2170,
        2363
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ],
